This project builds on the work below. Nothing from it is copied into this repository unless noted;
it is used as a dependency, a tool, or a specification.

- OrchardZSA (ZIP 226 / ZIP 227) reference implementation by QEDIT:
  https://github.com/QED-it/orchard (MIT OR Apache-2.0),
  https://github.com/QED-it/librustzcash (MIT OR Apache-2.0),
  https://github.com/QED-it/zebra (Apache-2.0 / MIT).
- zcash_tx_tool by QEDIT, https://github.com/QED-it/zcash_tx_tool, used as a library dependency
  (fetched by Cargo, not copied here) for block submission. Its README states it is licensed under the
  MIT License. Its crate pins are repeated in Cargo.toml, and its Cargo.lock was the starting point of
  ours.
- The Zcash protocol crates by Electric Coin Co. and the Zcash Foundation (MIT / Apache-2.0).
- ZIP 226 and ZIP 227, by Pablo Kogan, Vivek Arte, Daira-Emma Hopwood and Jack Grigg:
  https://zips.z.cash/zip-0226, https://zips.z.cash/zip-0227
- The Cachet metadata format v1, by the Cachet contributors (MIT):
  https://github.com/cachet-zec/cachet/blob/main/packages/registry-spec/README.md
  Our implementation of the format is written independently from its specification.
- ZMD-1 by ZecBit (MIT), compared in docs/METADATA.md: https://github.com/Zecbit-nft/zmd1
- The Sapling proving parameters (sapling-spend.params, sapling-output.params) are downloaded from
  https://download.z.cash and checked by SHA-256; they are not in this repository.
- FROST(secp256k1, SHA-256) with BIP-340 signatures, frost-secp256k1-tr by the Zcash Foundation
  (MIT OR Apache-2.0): https://github.com/ZcashFoundation/frost, used as a library dependency for the
  threshold issuer. FROST is specified in RFC 9591.
- Solana devnet helpers use @solana/web3.js (MIT) and @solana/spl-token (Apache-2.0).
- Other Rust dependencies are under permissive licenses: mostly MIT and/or Apache-2.0, plus
  BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, Zlib, CC0-1.0 and Unicode-3.0. See Cargo.lock.
